<title>UK: CYCLING-KELLY WINS WORLD TIME TRIAL TITLE.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-KELLY WINS WORLD TIME TRIAL TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shane Kelly of Australia retained the world one-kilometre time trial title at the world track championships on Wednesday, with a track record time of one minute 2.777 seconds.</p>
<p>Kelly averaged 57.345 kph to beat Soren Lausgberg of Germany by eighteen hundredths of a second. The bronze medal went to another German, Jan Van Eijden, in 1:04.541.</p>
</text>
